        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: beta releases require manual reruns after plugin publication",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe 2026.7.2 beta release path took many hours because independent validation, platform, npm, and plugin-registry work was repeatedly serialized or rerun. A beta could remain blocked on plugin ecosystem convergence even after the core release was already safe to publish.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Freezes a product-complete Code SHA and reuses its validation evidence instead of revalidating moving metadata.\n- Runs independent release readiness and cross-OS work concurrently with explicit caps, caching, timing, and resumable evidence.\n- Classifies evidence impact so docs/workflow metadata does not invalidate product proof.\n- Makes beta verification report live, degraded, or failed states without treating small plugin-registry lag as a core beta blocker.\n- Publishes prerelease core first, then moves plugin npm to ClawHub convergence into a detached trusted continuation. Stable releases, explicit wait mode, and plugin-only releases remain blocking.\n- Keeps the detached path safe: immutable parent-bound handoff, authenticated child identity artifacts, attempt-bound retry deduplication, cancellation cleanup, ambiguous-dispatch reconciliation, terminal repair, and always-uploaded evidence.\n- Uses GitHub's supported `return_run_details` workflow-dispatch response to bind run IDs immediately; ambiguous responses still fail closed and reconcile by authenticated correlation. Contract: https://github.blog/changelog/2026-02-19-workflow-dispatch-api-now-returns-run-ids/\n- Removes the no-op ShellCheck subprocess from actionlint, and makes sticky dependency snapshots self-healing: readers retain the fast exact-fingerprint path, while the canonical main writer reconciles and republishes the tree before fanout.\n\n## User Impact\n\nExpected beta critical path: roughly 15–30 minutes plus platform publish variability, instead of waiting for the entire plugin ecosystem. Plugin convergence continues asynchronously and remains visible/repairable. Stable release confidence is unchanged: required ecosystem work still blocks.\n\nNo release was created by this optimization work. `2026.7.2-beta.3` predates these final pipeline changes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased main: `c95a8e3df1e6e8d1ea4925b615707bc97f6f52b5`\n- Current head: `5b6730e7f649ed170c064631f3a7535383f460e1`\n- Release-focused suite: 516/516 passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29678303536\n- Rebased-head planner/config contract: 117/117 passed on Testbox `tbx_01kxx277en2wkvbby1ex2367hx`: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29685222874\n- Rebased-head `test:changed`: green in 4m32; 6,462 tooling tests plus Codex and memory extension shards passed\n- Current exact-head `check:changed`: green in 8m44 on Testbox `tbx_01kxx3sefsqwsb51db41k9db5n`; SDK surface/baseline, boundaries, format, typecheck, lint, and import-cycle checks passed\n- Full `actionlint` stopped hanging after disabling its already-ignored ShellCheck integration; structural workflow lint now completes locally in under one second\n- Workflow-sanity fix: 93/93 focused tests passed on Testbox `tbx_01kxx11355sh49ahy92h45gx0v`; scoped changed gate passed in 1m32\n- Sticky snapshot repair contract: 87/87 focused tests passed; the previous current-main CI and first PR CI failed the same seven jobs from an incomplete `ipaddr.js` importer tree, while exact-head CI passed completely after the one-time fingerprint invalidation and writer reconciliation: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29686076169\n- Embedded Bash syntax checks, `oxfmt`, and `git diff --check`: passed\n- Mandatory autoreview: clean after iterating through cancellation, retry, artifact-authentication, run-attempt race, planner ownership, actionlint, generated-baseline, and sticky-cache findings\n\nOperational timing evidence also confirmed the intended workflow: warm lease reuse avoids repeated 60–100 second hydration/sync costs, while focused workflow tests themselves take about 3.4 seconds.\n",
        "branch": "fix/forward-port-2026.7.2-release",
